{
  "action": "observe",
  "thought": "Layer 2 resolved most object chains but early-stage adjacent placement needs direct visual verification rather than action-template inference. I will focus symmetrically on Videos 4 and 1, comparing the same individual cutlet state: compact/unseasoned-under-plastic/tenderized versus exposed/flattened/seasoned. This will verify whether the visible operated-object state supports Video4 before Video1 or the reverse.",
  "params": {
    "observation_targets": [
      {
        "video_index": 4,
        "start_time": 0,
        "end_time": 32,
        "num_frames": 12
      },
      {
        "video_index": 1,
        "start_time": 0,
        "end_time": 16,
        "num_frames": 12
      }
    ],
    "focus_prompt": "MODE=focus. Use exactly 12 frames per video. Inherit confirmed context: Video6 creates separated raw cutlets; Video4 operates on a raw strip under plastic with mallet; Video1 operates on an exposed thin raw cutlet with seasoning grinder/hand press. Current uncertainty: the exact state direction between tenderizing and seasoning must be supported visually, not assumed. Compare Video4 and Video1 symmetrically on the same individual cutlet dimensions: plastic wrap present/absent, compact vs flattened thickness, mallet indentations/ridges, seasoning specks present/absent, exposed moist surface vs covered surface, board residue/contact traces, and tool-contact marks. Evidence that Video4 is earlier: Video4 cutlet is unseasoned/covered/being flattened and Video1 cutlet is uncovered/flatter/seasoned speckled. Evidence that Video1 is earlier: Video4 shows later-state traces such as seasoning under plastic, already speckled surface, or re-tenderizing after seasoning. Check for contradictions in both directions. Output concise comparison with event role, operation flow, object-state evidence, and remaining uncertainty."
  },
  "context_update": {
    "confirmed": [
      "Layer2 confirms Video6 whole roast slicing; Video5 coating; Video2 frying; Video3 clean butter-only pan."
    ],
    "dimensions_to_compare": [
      "plastic wrap present vs absent",
      "compact vs flattened thickness",
      "mallet indentations/ridges",
      "seasoning specks present vs absent",
      "exposed moist surface vs covered surface",
      "board/tool contact traces"
    ],
    "next_object_focus": [
      "individual cutlet in Videos4 and 1"
    ],
    "uncertain_visual_states": [
      "early-stage direction between Video4 tenderizing and Video1 seasoning",
      "Video3 vs Video2 pan relation direct continuity",
      "Video5-to-Video3 insertion remains to be visually justified if possible"
    ]
  }
}

{
  "action": "observe",
  "thought": "The early meat-prep direction Video4 -> Video1 is now visually supported. I still should not finalize until the cooking-stage adjacency is supported by object-state evidence, especially the pan/fat chain and whether the coating stage can be connected to pan preparation. I will focus symmetrically on Videos 5 and 3 first, because this is the less direct transition: coating completed in Video5 versus clean-pan butter preparation in Video3. I will ask for shared object/scene continuity such as the butter tub and whether the breaded cutlet state in Video5 is completed while Video3 has no cutlet yet but fat is being prepared.",
  "params": {
    "observation_targets": [
      {
        "video_index": 5,
        "start_time": 0,
        "end_time": 100,
        "num_frames": 12
      },
      {
        "video_index": 3,
        "start_time": 0,
        "end_time": 18,
        "num_frames": 12
      }
    ],
    "focus_prompt": "MODE=focus. Use exactly 12 frames per video. Inherit confirmed context: Video6 slices raw roast into cutlets; Video4 tenderizes an unseasoned cutlet under plastic; Video1 seasons an exposed flattened cutlet; Video5 coats a flattened cutlet in wet orange-yellow mixture and dry breadcrumbs; Video3 shows a clean pan with butter/margarine only; Video2 later shows a breaded cutlet frying in foamy fat. Current uncertainty: the visual state relation between Video5 coating completion and Video3 pan-fat preparation must be assessed without assuming recipe order. Compare Videos 5 and 3 symmetrically on these dimensions: (1) breaded cutlet presence/absence and completion state; (2) wet batter and breadcrumb bowls present/used/dirty vs absent; (3) butter/margarine tub appearance, open/closed/full/depleted/position, and whether it is the same container; (4) frying pan state absent/not in use vs clean empty pan receiving butter; (5) transfer traces/residue that indicate coating completed before pan prep or pan prep before coating. Evidence that Video5 is earlier: Video5 ends with meat newly crumb-coated and butter tub available/unused nearby, while Video3 uses that butter in a clean pan before cutlet/crumb residue appears. Evidence that Video3 is earlier: Video5 shows later traces of already-used pan/fat, depleted butter from prior pan use, or breadcrumb/coating happening after pan butter has already been prepared. Check contradictions in both directions. Output concise comparison with event role, operation flow, object-state evidence, and remaining uncertainty."
  },
  "context_update": {
    "confirmed": [
      "Focused comparison supports Video4 -> Video1: covered unseasoned compact strip being flattened becomes uncovered flattened seasoned cutlet."
    ],
    "resolved_uncertain": [
      "early-stage direction between Video4 tenderizing and Video1 seasoning resolved visually as Video4 before Video1"
    ],
    "dimensions_to_compare": [
      "breaded cutlet presence/absence and completed coating state",
      "batter/breadcrumb bowls used or absent",
      "butter/margarine tub continuity and depletion/use state",
      "frying pan absent/not in use vs clean pan receiving butter",
      "coating residue vs pan-fat residue"
    ],
    "next_object_focus": [
      "breaded cutlet and butter tub in Videos5 and 3"
    ],
    "uncertain_visual_states": [
      "Video5-to-Video3 insertion remains to be visually justified if possible",
      "Video3 vs Video2 pan relation direct continuity"
    ]
  }
}

{
  "action": "observe",
  "thought": "The Video5 -> Video3 relation is visually favored but still partly inferential; the remaining decisive cooking-stage chain is Video3 vs Video2. I will focus symmetrically on the frying pan/fat and breaded cutlet state to verify whether clean butter-only pan precedes used foamy pan with breaded cutlet, or whether Video3 could be a later/reset pan state. This directly addresses the remaining uncertain item before finalizing.",
  "params": {
    "observation_targets": [
      {
        "video_index": 3,
        "start_time": 0,
        "end_time": 18,
        "num_frames": 12
      },
      {
        "video_index": 2,
        "start_time": 0,
        "end_time": 52,
        "num_frames": 12
      }
    ],
    "focus_prompt": "MODE=focus. Use exactly 12 frames per video. Inherit confirmed context: Video6 slices a whole raw roast into cutlets; Video4 tenderizes an unseasoned cutlet under plastic; Video1 seasons an exposed flattened cutlet; Video5 coats a flattened cutlet in batter and breadcrumbs; Video3 shows clean pan receiving butter/margarine; Video2 shows a breaded cutlet frying and browning. Remaining uncertainty: Video3 vs Video2 pan/fat continuity and state direction. Compare Videos 3 and 2 symmetrically on the same operated objects: frying pan interior, fat/butter state, breaded cutlet presence/absence, crumb residue, bubbling/foam intensity, browning stage, utensil/tongs contact, and any reset/cleaning evidence. Evidence that Video3 is earlier: Video3 pan is clean/empty with only newly melting butter and no crumbs/cutlet, while Video2 has a breaded cutlet in hot foamy fat with crumb debris and browning. Evidence that Video2 is earlier: Video3 would need to show later/reset traces such as browned crumb residue removed, used oil remnants, cooked cutlet already removed, or a second butter addition to a dirty pan. Check contradictions in both directions. Output concise comparison with event role, operation flow, object-state evidence, and remaining uncertainty."
  },
  "context_update": {
    "confirmed": [
      "Focused comparison supports Video5 before Video3 more strongly than reverse: Video5 has coating bowls and newly crumbed cutlet with butter tub unused nearby; Video3 has clean pan receiving butter with no cutlet/crumbs."
    ],
    "resolved_uncertain": [
      "Video5-to-Video3 insertion visually favored as coating preparation before pan-fat preparation, though direct transfer not shown"
    ],
    "dimensions_to_compare": [
      "frying pan clean vs used",
      "newly melting butter vs foamy frying fat",
      "breaded cutlet absent vs present",
      "crumb residue absent vs present",
      "raw/pale crumb coating vs browned crust",
      "reset/cleaning evidence or lack thereof"
    ],
    "next_object_focus": [
      "frying pan/fat in Videos3 and 2",
      "breaded cutlet presence and browning in Videos3 and 2"
    ],
    "uncertain_visual_states": [
      "Video3 vs Video2 pan relation direct continuity"
    ]
